From 840c4e3d8f681441982c84b817ec782c74c1c278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Levine <blahm1d@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 17:22:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] core: P0015 - implement MOVE *Rs(SOff),*Rd(DOff)
 (mem-to-mem offset move)

The TMS34010 MOVE *Rs(SAddr),*Rd(DAddr) -- memory-to-memory with two
signed 16-bit bit-displacements (0xB800 F=0 / 0xBA00 F=1, 3-word encoding:
opcode + SOff + DOff) -- was never decoded. Same family as P0014's
abs-to-abs: birdybro implemented the offset store (0xB000) and load
(0xB400) but not the 0xB800 M2M form.

THE COIN PATH USES IT: the game reads coins as the upper half of a 32-bit
read at 0x01C00000 spanning {IN1,IN0} (why no absolute IN1 reference
exists). Inserting a coin fires the coin handler: coin-sound latch writes
(0xFD50/0xFF50), then ILLEGAL OPCODE at ffe61000: b800 0010 0020 =
MOVE *A0(10h),*A0(20h),0.

Fix: iclass INSTR_MOVE_OFF_M2M; decode top6 101110; CORE_FETCH_IMM_LO
routes to CORE_FETCH_IMM2_LO for the 16-bit DOff (exits straight to
EXECUTE, no HI word); two-step CORE_MEMORY read at Rs+sext(SOff) ->
write at Rd+sext(DOff), reusing the P0014 machinery.

VERIFIED (tb_yunit_state, 30M cycles): coin at 24M -> coin sound -> NO
illegal opcode -> CMOS credit/audit records written in the Williams
value+complement format (@01400090<=1 coin counter, @01401100<=1,
@014010e0<=1 with 0xff/0xffff/0xfe complements) -> game continues clean.
THE GAME COINS UP. MM TBs + tb_yunit_mem/memsys/dma PASS.

Also fixes tb_immi_il's stale SUBI/CMPI vectors (pre-existing debt from
P0008: the immediates must be stored one's-complemented, like the P0003
ANDI vector fix). tb_immi_il now PASSES.

